Phase 3A – Data Cleaning
Overview

Worked with messy data using PySpark to understand the importance of data cleaning in real-world scenarios.

Work Done
Identified data issues such as null values, duplicates, and invalid entries
Cleaned data using:
dropna() for removing null records
fillna() for handling missing values
filter() for removing invalid data
dropDuplicates() for eliminating duplicate rows
Validated data by checking row counts before and after cleaning
Performed aggregation to calculate customers per city
Learnings
Real-world data is often messy and inconsistent
Data cleaning is a critical step before analysis
Poor quality data leads to incorrect results and insights
Reflection

Cleaning data is essential to ensure accurate analysis and better decision-making.